vit_patch_drop
==============

A Vision Transformer that can drop input patches, used by the vision
benchmarks' arch_mod method (experiments/vision/vit_patch_drop_outputs.py).
It is not part of the MIT-licensed mcal package.

Origins
-------

src/models/vision_transformer.py, src/models/helpers.py, src/models/layers/
    Derived from PyTorch Image Models (timm),
    https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
    "Hacked together by / Copyright 2020 Ross Wightman".
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE in this
    directory.

Patch-dropping changes to those files
    Taken from https://github.com/madrylab/missingness, the code for
    Jain et al., "Missingness Bias in Model Debugging", ICLR 2022.
    That repository does not publish a licence.

src/models/load_trained_weights.py
    Written for MCal.

Changes made here
-----------------

Relative to madrylab/missingness, this copy removes the unused config
package (src/config/), the ResNet model (src/models/resnet.py), the
model-building helpers in src/models/__init__.py, and a debugger import
in src/models/vision_transformer.py.
